---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description={`The twelve-week teaching schedule: what happens in each ${sessionLabels.singular.toLowerCase()}, what to prepare, and what leaves the room.`}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Every week has a Lobby Lab on the Thursday, three days after its Monday
    lecture. In weeks 4, 8 and 11 that puts it the day before an assignment is
    due, which is deliberate: the last chance to ask a question in person is
    always in the room.
  </p>
  <p>
    A Lobby Lab is a different thing from a lecture, not a repeat of it. The
    lecture answers what the week's decision is and what mechanics sit behind
    it; the lab answers whether you can actually do it yet. Each one is a
    drill with a pass condition you could judge from the next seat, and each
    one needs other people — somebody to count your last hits, an opponent
    contesting the lane, four teammates to call to, a rival captain across the
    draft. A drill you could do alone at home would be homework, and we would
    have set it as homework.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where a drill needs a quantity — a round length, a number of wards, a
    replay to watch — the tutor sets it in the room, on the day. Individual
    labs below just say that the tutor sets it.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
